NNAAMMEE
     mmaacc__tteesstt — MAC framework testing policy

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile the testing policy into your kernel, place the following lines
     in your kernel configuration file:

           ooppttiioonnss MMAACC
           ooppttiioonnss MMAACC__TTEESSTT

     Alternately, to load the testing module at boot time, place the following
     line in your kernel configuration file:

           ooppttiioonnss MMAACC

     and in loader.conf(5):

           mac_test_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmaacc__tteesstt policy module implements a testing facility for the MAC
     framework.  Among other things, mmaacc__tteesstt will try to catch corrupt labels
     the system is attempting to destroy and drop to the debugger.  Addition‐
     ally, a set of statistics regarding the number of times various MAC
     framework entry points have been called is stored in the
     _s_e_c_u_r_i_t_y_._m_a_c_._t_e_s_t sysctl(8) tree.

   LLaabbeell FFoorrmmaatt
     No labels are defined for mmaacc__tteesstt.

